From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:01:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Embedding: raise #AC while RFLAGS.AC is set

x86 raises #AC at CPL 3 for a misaligned access while RFLAGS.AC is set,
and an embedding host that runs x86 programs exactly needs to know
when. The floating-point mode an embedder sets now also says whether
RFLAGS.AC is set, and POPF and IRET leave a context whose mode they
change, after writing back what they retire.

In that mode every access of two, four or eight bytes checks that its
address is a multiple of its size, before its translation, and leaves
with EMBEDDER_EXIT_ALIGNMENT_FAULT when it is not; the instruction has
changed nothing. A pair checks each operand by its size. The elements
of a masked vector move, as parts of a wider operand, and of a gather
check nothing. A new EmbedderAlignmentCheck op checks an operand x86
checks as a whole: an x87 environment or state image by the width of
its fields, before FLDENV or FRSTOR probes it, IRET's and POPA's stack
before the probe of their frame, and the operand of a bit test, which
the frontend reads as a byte. It also exempts the rest of FXSAVE,
FXRSTOR, XSAVE, XRSTOR, FNSAVE, FRSTOR, FNSTENV, FLDENV and the indirect
far transfers. A REP MOVS or STOS is the host's to check.
